# The build context of every image (WP-7): default deny. Everything is out unless a line below
# lets it back in, so a new root file (an editor or agent config, a local note, a key) never enters
# a build by accident: least privilege for the context, and no local secret can reach a layer
# (ADR-043). The images need the workspace manifests and the sources; each builds its own dist.
*

# What the three Dockerfiles copy (`COPY package.json pnpm-lock.yaml pnpm-workspace.yaml`, then
# `COPY . .` for the build): the workspace manifests, turbo's task graph and the sources. Every
# workspace folder in pnpm-workspace.yaml must be here (templates/ too), or the frozen install fails.
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!turbo.json
!apps/
!packages/
!templates/

# Excluded again inside the re-included folders: the last matching line wins, so these come after.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets: every env file, the committed templates too. No image needs them.
**/.env
**/.env.*
